   "data": {
    "text": "In `lagos-lekki-v1` for `120mm / 3h` storm:\n\n* Baseline: `baseline 120mm/3h` - run `r_3277ec9d2e6e1ec8`\n* Tide-lock: same storm + `tide boundary_level_m: 1.0 m` - run `r_cc14fcd1e804a1f0`\n\nThis is a planning model, not a forecast.\n\n### Flooded buildings\n\n> Tide-lock holds water in the system - outflow reverses and stored volume rises by ~6.46M m3.\n\n* `buildings_flooded`: 30,202 -> 30,595 = **+393 buildings, +1.3%**\n* `buildings_flooded_severe`: 9,187 -> 9,544 = **+357, +3.9%**\n* `people_exposed`: 94,280 -> 96,288 = **+2,008, +2.1%**\n* `road_km_impassable`: 406.713 km -> 450.011 km = **+43.298 km, +10.6%**\n* `flooded_area_km2`: 23.1791 -> 29.7909 = **+6.6118 km2, +28.5%**\n* `max_depth_m`: 2.154 m -> 2.154 m = **no change**\n\nIn `Lekki Phase 1` specifically, almost no change:\n\n* `area:Lekki Phase 1:buildings_flooded`: 1,614 -> 1,612\n* `area:Lekki Phase 1:people_exposed`: 5,129 -> 5,122\n* `area:Lekki Phase 1:road_km_impassable`: 19.678 km -> 19.71 km\n\ni.e. the +393 buildings study-area-wide is not in Phase 1, it is lagoon-side / low-lying storage expansion.\n\n### Evacuation route to nearest shelter\n\nTested from `Lekki Phase 1 [3.47674,6.44154]` to nearest shelter.\n\nNearest shelter found in both runs: `Lekki British School (candidate shelter (assumed))`\n\n**At t=3600s - 1h into storm:**\n\n* Baseline `rt_7a2ae075cc3c`: reachable=true, length 0.865 km, ETA 13.0 min, edges_removed 48\n* Tide-lock `rt_cdab0094fe42`: reachable=true, length 0.865 km, ETA 13.0 min, edges_removed 363\n\n> Same path, same shelter, same time early - but tide-lock has already removed +315 road edges network-wide.\n\n**At peak t=10200s:**\n\n* Baseline `rt_a6a760f4a2e1`: reachable=false, edges_removed 2773\n* Tide-lock `rt_1ddc055b81a2`: reachable=false, edges_removed 3103\n\n> By peak, evacuation from this origin is cut off in **both** cases. Tide-lock makes it worse by +330 blocked edges.\n\nEngineering takeaway: 1 m lagoon hold does not much change building flooding in Phase 1, but study-area-wide it adds ~357 severe buildings, +43.3 km impassable roads and +6.6 km2 flooded area, and degrades the road network earlier - leave before peak."
